WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
Every test passed.

2
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.040
So the code is ready, right?

3
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.600
CrossExam asks a harder question: what did those tests miss?

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.000
OpenAI wrote this optimization.

5
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.160
It passes all four tests.

6
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.640
But one customer reserves two units, and another customer's stock drops too.

7
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.160
Two requests prove it.

8
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.280
Then it writes stronger tests in a separate context.

9
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.200
Detection jumps from one to four, then climbs to seven.

10
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.840
Every promotion has to pass the same gate.

11
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.640
Now freeze the tests and open the final audit.

12
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.400
6 of 8 bugs caught.

13
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.360
2 missed.

14
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.600
All four correct implementations still pass.

15
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.920
Subquadratic chooses where to look.

16
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.880
OpenAI makes the proposals.

17
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.040
OpenUI shows the evidence.

18
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.320
One real run, on a small synthetic benchmark.

19
00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:47.520
CrossExam.

20
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.160
Passing tests should mean something.
